messages.content:
You are supporting a process mining research prototype.
Use only the synthetic scenario information provided below.
Do not invent company-specific system names, product names, confidential logs, internal metrics, or real organizational details.
Return valid JSON only. Do not wrap it in Markdown.

Scenario ID: S02
Scenario title: Equipment-Specific Measurement Workflow
Initial workflow description:
A wafer is measured using one of several tools. The exact preparation and measurement steps differ by tool, and the engineer records the result after measurement.

Clarification questions:
[
  {
    "id": "Q1",
    "question": "What determines which measurement tool is used for a given wafer—for example, is it based on wafer type, lot specification, tool availability, or some other criterion?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q2",
    "question": "Can you walk through the preparation and measurement steps for each tool variant, listing the distinct actions an operator must perform from the moment the wafer arrives at the tool until measurement is complete?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q3",
    "question": "How does the engineer record the measurement result—what medium or system is used, and what data fields are captured at that point?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q4",
    "question": "What happens after the measurement result is recorded—are there defined thresholds or criteria that determine whether the wafer passes, is reworked, or is scrapped?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q5",
    "question": "Besides the engineer who records the result, which other roles or systems are involved in the workflow, and what actions are they responsible for?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q6",
    "question": "What event triggers the start of this measurement workflow, and how is the wafer physically or informationally handed off between each step or actor?"
  }
]
Reference workflow for oracle use:
{
  "goal": "Measure a wafer using the appropriate equipment-specific procedure and record the result.",
  "actors": [
    "measurement engineer",
    "equipment owner",
    "requester"
  ],
  "systems": [
    "measurement equipment",
    "equipment reservation system",
    "measurement result repository"
  ],
  "inputs": [
    "measurement request",
    "wafer identifier",
    "measurement recipe",
    "equipment availability"
  ],
  "outputs": [
    "measurement result",
    "equipment usage record",
    "request completion notice"
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "id": "A1",
      "name": "Confirm measurement request and wafer identifier",
      "actor": "measurement engineer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A2",
      "name": "Select suitable measurement equipment",
      "actor": "measurement engineer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A3",
      "name": "Check equipment availability and reserve slot",
      "actor": "measurement engineer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A4",
      "name": "Prepare wafer according to equipment procedure",
      "actor": "measurement engineer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A5",
      "name": "Run measurement recipe",
      "actor": "measurement engineer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A6",
      "name": "Validate measurement output",
      "actor": "measurement engineer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A7",
      "name": "Upload result and notify requester",
      "actor": "measurement engineer"
    }
  ],
  "decisions": [
    {
      "id": "D1",
      "condition": "Which equipment is required for the requested measurement?",
      "branches": [
        "equipment type A",
        "equipment type B",
        "equipment type C"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "D2",
      "condition": "Is the equipment available and qualified?",
      "branches": [
        "available",
        "unavailable or under maintenance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "D3",
      "condition": "Is the measurement output valid?",
      "branches": [
        "valid",
        "invalid or noisy"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "exceptions": [
    "equipment unavailable",
    "wafer information mismatch",
    "recipe not approved",
    "invalid measurement output"
  ],
  "dependencies": [
    {
      "from": "A1",
      "to": "A2",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A2",
      "to": "A3",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A3",
      "to": "A4",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A4",
      "to": "A5",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A5",
      "to": "A6",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A6",
      "to": "A7",
      "type": "control_flow"
    }
  ],
  "automation_opportunities": [
    {
      "target": "A2",
      "rationale": "Equipment selection can be recommended from measurement type and wafer condition."
    },
    {
      "target": "A3",
      "rationale": "Reservation checks can be automated through system integration."
    },
    {
      "target": "A6",
      "rationale": "Output validity can be partially checked using rule-based thresholds or historical patterns."
    }
  ]
}
Task: Simulate a concise domain expert who answers only these questions using the reference workflow.
Do not reveal the full reference workflow. Do not add details not needed by the questions.
If a requested fact is absent, explicitly say it is not specified; do not guess.
Use at most 80 words per answer. Return one answer for each question, with matching ID and question text.
Return JSON: {"answers": [{"question_id": "Q1", "question": "original question", "answer": "grounded answer"}]}

Additional constraint for this respondent: this expert answers vaguely and never commits to specifics.
Do not name any actor, system, artifact, threshold, condition or exception from the reference workflow.
Use hedged generalities such as "the person in charge usually checks it before it goes out".
Answer every question in this style, at most 30 words each.
